  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Boeing Joint Project Office recorded $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Bell Boeing Joint Project Office received 1,216 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.1M, and obligations are up 1.5% year over year. Historical obligations show peaks and troughs: FY21 had $2.5B, FY22 had $1.9B, FY23 had $947M, FY24 had $871M, FY25 had $1.4B, and FY26 has $1.4B to date. The Department of Defense accounted for the largest buying agency of record with $1.4B in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration with $2.1M. Market concentration is heavy in aerospace and related services: Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing totaled $822M and Aircraft Manufacturing totaled $499M. Smaller market lines include Computer Systems Design Services at $37.6M and several niche manufacturing categories ranging from $7.9M down to negative values, reflecting accounting adjustments in one category. These figures are contract obligations unless otherwise noted for award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
